        "original_id": "281cc807-b831-5d2d-beb5-9be36774a886",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gil Hibben, Ed Parker\n- Products: Browning hunting knives, American Kenpo Knife, Rambo Knife\n- Topics: American Kenpo, custom knifemaking, martial arts\n- Places: Wyoming, La Grange, Kentucky\n- Events: Rambo, Rambo III\n\nFacts:\n- Gil Hibben was born on September 4, 1935.\n- Gil Hibben is an American custom knifemaker from Wyoming who is based in La Grange, Kentucky.\n- In 1968, Gil Hibben designed the first line of Browning hunting knives.\n- Gil Hibben designed the American Kenpo Knife for Ed Parker.\n- Gil Hibben designed the Rambo Knife for the films \"Rambo\" and \"Rambo III.\"\n- American Kenpo is a martial art characterized by quick and powerful strikes delivered with the body’s natural weapons and powered by rapid stance transitions.",
